    "body": "## Problem\n\n`tests/test_agent/test_swe_workspace_diff.py::test_patch_uses_actual_image_baseline_without_changing_git_index` is flaky on CI. Example: https://github.com/THUDM/slime/actions/runs/38288879812 (job `agent-test (0, test_agent/test_swe_workspace_diff.py)`):\n\n```\nshutil.Error: [('.../agent repo/.git/objects/maintenance.lock', '.../grader repo/.git/objects/maintenance.lock', \"[Errno 2] No such file or directory: ...\")]\n```\n\nThe runner has git 2.55. After the test's `git commit`, git starts auto-maintenance in the background, which creates and then deletes `.git/objects/maintenance.lock`. The next line, `shutil.copytree(repo, fresh)`, sometimes lists the lock file and then fails because it's gone before the copy reaches it.\n\n## Fix\n\nTurn off auto-maintenance and auto-gc in the temporary test repo (`maintenance.auto=false`, `gc.auto=0`) right after `git init`. The test only uses this repo as a fixture, so nothing it checks depends on maintenance.\n\n## Testing\n\nRan `pytest tests/test_agent/test_swe_workspace_diff.py` locally 3 times with the CI agent-test dependency set on Python 3.10; 3/3 passed each run.",
    "changed_files": 1,
